  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<div class="editor-indent">
  <para>1. Which of these scatter plots shows data that would best be modeled with a linear function? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
</div>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-justify-content-between">
      <para>Graph A 
        
           <figure><media alt="Scatterplot."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a2cffe2402ce74466cff9ac61ce61ebe2133f218"/></media></figure></para>
           <para>Graph B
       
           <figure><media alt="Scatter plot."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/de0a019009ffffea916b212daa4e99a1b8c71862"/></media></figure></para>
     </div>
  </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Graph B. Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. The points in scatter plot B seem to follow the shape of a line of best fit. The points in scatter plot in A are very spread out.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
   <para>Which of the following lines is most likely the line of best fit for the data provided?</para>
